\newlabel{fig:dataset_differences}{{8}{12}{Plots showing the mean and standard deviation of the FTIR spectral intensities across each class. The cancerous sample spectra are seen to have slightly smaller standard deviations than other classifications. The only visually discernable difference between the mean spectra is around 1120 cm$^{-1}$, where the cancerous spectra does not show a small peak which can be observed in the spectra associated with the other classes}{figure.8}{}}
